# Rust / Tauri build artifacts
src-tauri/target
src-tauri/gen
# NOTE: src-tauri/Cargo.lock is intentionally TRACKED (committed), not ignored.
# The Mezzanine ships as a binary, so the lockfile must pin the exact
# dependency tree the release builds — Rust's own guidance for applications.
# It was ignored until v0.2.5, when the release regenerated the lock fresh and
# drifted onto a broken `tauri-utils 2.9.2` (E0119 conflict with `time`) that
# never compiles, failing the Ascent build while local stayed green on 2.9.1.
# Committing the lock makes the release reproducible. See mezzanine-debugging.md.

# Tauri runtime caches
src-tauri/.cache

# The Ascent (#00056) — updater signing keys. The private key is the
# security spine: lose it and no future build can ever update an installed
# balcony. It is escrowed by the investor (password manager + GitHub Actions
# secrets) and NEVER committed. The public key lives in tauri.conf.json under
# plugins.updater.pubkey — not as a loose file. RD-4.
*.key
*.key.pub
.tauri-keys/

# Chronicle transcripts safeguard — canonical path is ~/.zmuuzn-cockpit/
# (outside any repo); these entries fire if the chronicle base ever drifts
# inside the gadget's working tree.
.zmuuzn-cockpit/
.zmuuzn-cockpit-transcripts/
